WEBVTT

00:01.790 --> 00:03.380
It's nice to meet you!

00:05.290 --> 00:07.960
The beastmen from Howling Village moved here.

00:08.380 --> 00:11.170
If you need anything, just ask Lamulias.
She's the housing manager.

00:11.170 --> 00:12.920
It's nice to meet you.

00:13.290 --> 00:14.380
Yes!

00:14.380 --> 00:16.630
Uh, you don't need to be that formal...

00:17.790 --> 00:19.630
Apparently, they all thought

00:19.630 --> 00:23.040
that they were going to be treated
horribly when they moved here.

00:23.790 --> 00:26.130
Naturally, we have no such intentions.

00:26.920 --> 00:30.630
There doesn't seem to be any apparent
problem with the new residents, however...

00:30.880 --> 00:31.790
However?

00:33.460 --> 00:35.080
They faint quite often.

00:35.080 --> 00:37.630
Well, they'll just have to get
used to things here.

00:47.790 --> 00:49.790
<b>Farming Life in Another World</b>

00:49.580 --> 00:57.170
Masshiro hikari no naka me o samashite
hajimatteiku sutoorii

00:57.170 --> 01:03.920
Fumidasu atarashii sekai donna hana o sakaseyou?

01:04.130 --> 01:11.500
Kumori sora datte mizutamari de yogoretatte

01:11.500 --> 01:14.330
Bokura wa susumu

01:14.330 --> 01:21.080
Souzou mo shinai mirai ga matteiru kitto

01:21.380 --> 01:24.960
Deatte deatte tsunagatteku

01:24.960 --> 01:28.250
Waraeba mawari mo egao ni naru

01:28.250 --> 01:32.290
Chiisana tane maite sodateyou

01:32.290 --> 01:36.380
Yagate ookina hana ni naru

01:36.380 --> 01:39.880
Koukai ya shippai wa kate ni shite

01:39.880 --> 01:43.170
Karafuru na shiawase de afureru youni

01:43.170 --> 01:47.420
Bokura te o toriatte wakeatte

01:47.420 --> 01:53.250
Sekaijuu ni hirogatteike Flower Ring

02:11.080 --> 02:11.960
Wait up!

02:11.960 --> 02:12.920
Come on!

02:19.250 --> 02:21.960
Jeez, you need to be
more careful when you play.

02:22.290 --> 02:24.250
You can use magic too, Sena?

02:24.250 --> 02:25.750
Yes, I can.

02:26.080 --> 02:29.630
Don't tell me... am I the only one here
who can't use magic?

02:29.630 --> 02:33.330
Well, all of the angels can use magic...

02:34.540 --> 02:35.540
Yes.

02:35.540 --> 02:37.630
All of the high elves can use magic.

02:39.250 --> 02:42.920
It's common for us to be able to use
fire and water magic.

02:43.290 --> 02:45.580
We're good with water.

02:50.540 --> 02:52.420
Even the bees can do it.

02:57.630 --> 02:59.130
Don't worry!

02:59.130 --> 03:01.130
You're not the only one
who can't use magic!

03:01.380 --> 03:03.130
Let's practice together.

03:03.130 --> 03:04.710
Yeah, you're right.

03:04.710 --> 03:07.080
I have a feeling these kids
will surpass me, too.

03:07.500 --> 03:10.500
Oh well. There's no point
in wishing for the impossible.

03:10.500 --> 03:12.790
I'll just focus on what I can do for now.

03:15.960 --> 03:17.670
What was that? An earthquake?

03:18.750 --> 03:19.630
Mayor!

03:20.290 --> 03:23.670
A grappler bear and a bloody viper are
fighting in the northern area of the forest!

03:23.670 --> 03:25.500
Bear and viper?

03:25.790 --> 03:27.830
A bear and a snake?

03:30.710 --> 03:33.790
Them fighting with each other is enough
to make the ground shake this much?

03:34.040 --> 03:35.130
What shall we do?

03:35.130 --> 03:38.130
Hm... a bear and a snake?

03:38.330 --> 03:40.880
If this keeps up, it might affect the village.

03:40.880 --> 03:44.130
But it would be dangerous to get
involved without a plan.

03:44.330 --> 03:45.750
That's true.

03:45.750 --> 03:47.170
So about those animals...

03:47.420 --> 03:48.960
do you think we can eat them?

03:51.540 --> 03:56.040
So anyways, I've heard that hunters
sometimes eat bear meat.

03:56.040 --> 03:58.460
I've always wondered how they taste.

03:58.460 --> 03:59.540
Okay...

04:00.540 --> 04:01.710
There they are!

04:06.080 --> 04:08.290
Wow, they're big.

04:09.460 --> 04:10.920
Let's go back for help!

04:10.920 --> 04:13.330
No. Just take me down really fast.

04:14.790 --> 04:16.000
Understood.

04:23.080 --> 04:25.000
It's been a while since I got a big one.

04:25.000 --> 04:27.250
One... Two...

04:27.250 --> 04:28.250
What's wrong?

04:28.250 --> 04:31.630
Could you take down a monster
like that with one attack?

04:31.630 --> 04:32.710
No way.

04:32.710 --> 04:35.630
Yeah... the mayor is something else.

04:36.920 --> 04:39.880
Looking at him up close, he really is huge.

04:40.080 --> 04:43.960
As far as cooking them goes,
what do you plan to make?

04:44.670 --> 04:46.000
I've got some ideas.

04:48.330 --> 04:51.170
I'll add in some of these herbs and spices.

04:51.170 --> 04:53.170
Now we add wine and simmer.

04:53.170 --> 04:54.920
Our precious wine?!

04:54.920 --> 04:57.290
It's fine. That kind of cooking is normal.

04:57.420 --> 05:02.130
<b>Wine Braised Grappler Bear</b>

04:58.210 --> 05:01.670
And there we have it,
wine braised grappler bear.

05:05.540 --> 05:07.420
It's incredibly gamey.

05:07.420 --> 05:09.250
Our precious wine...

05:09.250 --> 05:11.080
I'm telling you this is normal.

05:11.170 --> 05:15.670
<b>Chicken-fried Bloody Viper</b>

05:12.170 --> 05:14.130
And this is the blood viper.

05:14.130 --> 05:15.670
I tried frying it.

05:18.920 --> 05:20.750
This tastes just like fried chicken!

05:20.750 --> 05:22.210
It's great!

05:22.210 --> 05:24.000
It tastes different than I expected.

05:25.460 --> 05:27.380
It tastes surprisingly like chicken breast.

05:27.380 --> 05:31.080
Which means my plate is missing
something that goes right here.

05:31.210 --> 05:33.170
<b>Flora's Lab</b>

05:32.290 --> 05:35.210
So then, what brings you here today?

05:35.210 --> 05:38.500
I was wondering if you had anything
that could act as an anti-bacterial agent.

05:38.500 --> 05:39.960
Anti-bacterial?

05:39.960 --> 05:43.880
Yeah. I need it for a new recipe
I want to try.

05:44.580 --> 05:48.380
Do you have any medicines that can
kill harmful microorganisms?

05:48.380 --> 05:49.710
Microorganisms!

05:49.710 --> 05:51.830
Those are the things you spoke of before!

05:51.830 --> 05:53.460
Yeah, that's them.

05:53.710 --> 05:56.000
I want something that will prevent
stomach aches or illness.

05:56.000 --> 05:57.000
I see.

05:57.000 --> 05:58.630
Leave it to me!

05:58.880 --> 06:00.920
Ah, how about this one?

06:01.670 --> 06:04.500
One dose is enough to blast anything
to the other side of the mountains.

06:04.500 --> 06:06.710
Do you have anything that's more peaceful?

06:07.040 --> 06:08.540
Then how about this one?

06:08.880 --> 06:11.170
This one is safe to use in foods.

06:11.170 --> 06:12.830
Yeah, this will work.

06:12.830 --> 06:13.790
Thanks.

06:14.130 --> 06:15.130
Of course.

06:15.130 --> 06:17.710
By the way, how's the
miso production coming along?

06:18.420 --> 06:21.000
The truth is, it's not going very well.

06:21.000 --> 06:23.670
I did everything exactly like you told me to,

06:23.670 --> 06:27.250
but no matter how long I waited it never
seemed like it was starting to ferment.

06:31.170 --> 06:33.880
I've had to rebuild my hut three times.

06:33.880 --> 06:35.540
That's not supposed to happen.

06:35.880 --> 06:38.210
Well, let's give it another try.

06:38.210 --> 06:39.670
Can we?!

06:40.250 --> 06:42.330
I'll try to keep the explosives to a minimum!

06:42.330 --> 06:43.960
Please don't use any.

06:49.670 --> 06:51.580
There we go. That looks good.

06:53.880 --> 06:56.670
First, we beat the eggs.

06:57.040 --> 06:59.420
Then we add salt and vinegar.

06:59.880 --> 07:01.880
By the way, this vinegar
is made from apples.

07:01.880 --> 07:03.880
That's also fermented, right?

07:04.170 --> 07:07.630
Then we mix it as we slowly add in the oil.

07:07.830 --> 07:09.580
And now we have mayonnaise.

07:11.130 --> 07:13.750
Now it's exactly like having fried chicken!

07:14.250 --> 07:17.500
Wow! I can eat this stuff by itself!

07:17.960 --> 07:20.130
Stop that right now.
It's terrible for your health.

07:20.540 --> 07:22.960
Now then, on to making miso.

07:23.500 --> 07:26.670
First, we start by simmering
the soybeans we soaked in water.

07:26.670 --> 07:28.170
Then we grind them.

07:32.670 --> 07:34.750
Moldy, moldy, moldy, mold!

07:34.750 --> 07:35.080
Moldy, moldy, moldy...

07:35.080 --> 07:36.830
I used the almighty farming tool
to help make the koji mold.
Moldy, moldy, moldy...<b></b>

07:36.830 --> 07:37.790
I used the almighty farming tool
to help make the koji mold.
You don't need to write that down.<b></b>

07:37.790 --> 07:38.630
You don't need to write that down.

07:38.960 --> 07:41.540
We mixed the koji with salt
and formed balls.

07:43.210 --> 07:45.210
Now we pack it into barrels.

07:45.670 --> 07:46.790
I see.

07:47.210 --> 07:50.040
Mine didn't work because
I didn't say moldy, moldy, mold.

07:50.040 --> 07:52.500
No, that's... well, maybe.

07:53.420 --> 07:55.790
Now we just let it age in the cellar.

07:55.790 --> 07:58.500
It'll take a few months,
so let's wait patiently.

07:58.500 --> 08:00.040
That long?

08:00.250 --> 08:01.210
Yeah.

08:01.210 --> 08:04.040
But all that time will make
the flavors even more intense.

08:04.040 --> 08:06.630
This requires perseverance,
just like research.

08:06.630 --> 08:07.460
Yup.

08:07.460 --> 08:09.080
Ah, there you are.

08:09.080 --> 08:10.580
You've got visitors.

08:11.170 --> 08:12.170
Visitors?

08:13.670 --> 08:17.750
The visitors were a group of dwarves
led by a man named Donovan.

08:17.920 --> 08:19.630
We're elder dwarves.

08:19.630 --> 08:21.330
What's the difference?

08:21.330 --> 08:23.920
We've heard that you have
high quality alcohol in this village,

08:23.920 --> 08:25.960
and we'd like you to share some with us.

08:26.170 --> 08:27.630
You mean our wine?

08:27.630 --> 08:29.080
I'd be happy to share with you...

08:29.080 --> 08:32.000
Mayor. We can't give it away for free.

08:32.000 --> 08:32.830
Huh?

08:32.830 --> 08:35.670
She's right. Our wine is very valuable.

08:35.670 --> 08:37.960
Yeah, but they're our guests...

08:37.960 --> 08:40.290
I'm sorry, but we don't have money.

08:40.290 --> 08:42.880
However, we do have technology.

08:43.130 --> 08:44.170
Technology?

08:44.170 --> 08:45.250
That's right.

08:45.250 --> 08:48.000
We've spent our lives
studying alcohol production,

08:48.000 --> 08:50.250
and we've traveled a long way to get here.

08:50.250 --> 08:53.250
You have some very fine
crops in this village.

08:53.250 --> 08:56.250
We can help you turn them
into fine alcohol.

08:56.250 --> 08:59.210
What do you think?
Don't you want to drink some?

09:02.380 --> 09:05.920
Donovan and his men got to work
on the alcohol right away.

09:07.130 --> 09:10.750
Distillation... I remember doing this
in science class.

09:13.000 --> 09:15.080
Here you go. This is corn whiskey.

09:15.460 --> 09:17.130
It's crystal clear.

09:17.130 --> 09:20.250
It'll get its color when we
age it in barrels.

09:20.250 --> 09:21.460
I see.

09:23.540 --> 09:25.290
This is strong!

09:26.500 --> 09:29.250
I guess the mayor is a lightweight.

09:29.250 --> 09:33.290
Donovan and his men ended up staying
in the village and working as our brewers.

09:34.830 --> 09:36.830
Now that we've got new alcohol,

09:36.830 --> 09:39.790
it's time to have a welcome party for
the beastmen and the dwarves!

09:39.960 --> 09:41.460
Drink up, everyone!

09:46.080 --> 09:50.420
You can really taste the fragrance
when you drink this alcohol.

09:50.420 --> 09:52.790
I really like this mayonnaise.

09:53.670 --> 09:55.790
This goes perfect with the booze.

09:55.790 --> 09:58.000
Let's drink all night!

09:58.250 --> 09:59.790
He snuck in again...

09:59.790 --> 10:03.710
I don't mind that he comes here,
but he always drinks too much.

10:03.710 --> 10:08.130
Alright! It's time to show you all
my special technique!

10:11.130 --> 10:13.170
Thanks for everything, mayor.

10:13.170 --> 10:16.000
It was kind of you to take us all in.

10:16.000 --> 10:18.790
Don't mention it.
We're all happy you're here.

10:19.380 --> 10:22.420
Yeah, there are a lot of people
in this village who like to drink.

10:23.580 --> 10:28.540
Wait a minute, I finally got some
adult men to join the village.

10:29.290 --> 10:30.790
By the way, Donovan.

10:30.790 --> 10:33.210
I'm not asking for any particular reason, but...

10:34.000 --> 10:35.830
are there any girls here who catch your eye?

10:35.830 --> 10:38.540
You know, the kind that make you
think "Wow, she's pretty!"?

10:39.880 --> 10:42.040
Well they're all very good looking,

10:42.040 --> 10:46.250
but you know, I think they're all
a little too young for me...

10:46.250 --> 10:50.080
If they can't at least grow a beard,
then they're not for me.

10:51.000 --> 10:52.500
A-a beard?

10:52.500 --> 10:55.380
Man, why are you making me
say it out loud...

10:55.380 --> 10:57.290
The cultural barrier is high.

10:58.830 --> 10:59.670
Farming Life...

10:59.670 --> 11:00.710
in Anoooother...

11:00.710 --> 11:01.790
World.

11:15.420 --> 11:17.040
Don't tell me there's another wyvern.

11:17.250 --> 11:18.670
Wait, a dragon?!

11:19.130 --> 11:21.080
It's headed straight for us,

11:21.080 --> 11:22.920
and it doesn't look friendly.

11:22.920 --> 11:26.080
I'm going to finish this one off before it
causes any damage to the village.

11:30.130 --> 11:31.000
What?

11:31.290 --> 11:33.250
Isn't that... Dryme?!

11:33.420 --> 11:34.880
Is this infighting?

11:34.880 --> 11:37.080
But they're just staring each other down now.

11:39.380 --> 11:40.580
There's another one?!

11:42.000 --> 11:43.500
That one's dangerous!

11:48.130 --> 11:49.330
I missed...

11:51.130 --> 11:52.460
But the next one won't!

11:52.790 --> 11:54.250
Please wait!

11:54.250 --> 11:56.500
That isn't an enemy!

11:59.380 --> 12:01.920
I'm terribly sorry for the confusion.

12:02.250 --> 12:06.000
These two are my master's wife
and his daughter.

12:06.380 --> 12:08.330
I'm Lastismoon.

12:08.330 --> 12:10.460
My name is Graffaloon.

12:10.790 --> 12:13.250
N-nice to meet you. I'm Hiraku Machio.

12:13.710 --> 12:16.080
Why are your wife and daughter here?

12:16.080 --> 12:17.960
Well, you see...

12:17.960 --> 12:21.920
Apparently, Dryme's constant sneaking out
so that he could come to our village

12:21.920 --> 12:24.420
has roused some suspicions at home.

12:25.210 --> 12:29.170
What were we supposed to think
when he was sneaking out every night?

12:29.420 --> 12:32.250
If it turned out that he really was
sneaking out to do something he shouldn't...

12:34.630 --> 12:37.080
What a ridiculous accusation.

12:37.080 --> 12:40.330
But you were sneaking off with
all kinds of stuff from the treasury!

12:40.330 --> 12:42.290
And you'd always be out
till the next morning.

12:42.290 --> 12:44.290
Ah, I get it now.

12:44.290 --> 12:46.540
It's the gifts he always brings us.

12:46.540 --> 12:52.040
<b>Dryme's House</b>

12:47.040 --> 12:49.580
And I was worried about him
going home drunk, so I built him a house.

12:49.580 --> 12:51.790
Maybe that wasn't such a good idea.

12:52.290 --> 12:55.000
That was all for the sake of
our diplomatic relations!

12:55.000 --> 12:56.630
It was all very high-level politics,
you see, and uh...

12:56.630 --> 12:58.460
He's hiding something.
It was all very high-level politics,<b>
</b>you see, and uh...<b></b>

12:58.460 --> 12:59.330
Indeed.

12:59.630 --> 13:00.830
At this point...

13:00.830 --> 13:02.330
my suspicions...

13:02.330 --> 13:04.420
are all being confirmed.

13:04.420 --> 13:05.290
She's scary.

13:05.290 --> 13:06.830
Wait a minute, you two!

13:06.830 --> 13:07.830
Just think about it!

13:07.830 --> 13:09.080
Do you think this man...

13:09.080 --> 13:10.580
even has the courage...

13:10.580 --> 13:13.080
to have an affair like that?!

13:13.380 --> 13:14.750
That's a good point.

13:14.750 --> 13:16.210
Ah, thank goodness.

13:16.210 --> 13:17.630
Are you all happy with that?

13:17.790 --> 13:19.210
Um, excuse me.

13:19.210 --> 13:22.460
Even though I didn't know who you were,
I'm sorry about how I acted earlier.

13:22.460 --> 13:25.540
No, don't worry about it.
This was all our fault.

13:25.540 --> 13:28.170
Come on you two, apologize!

13:28.580 --> 13:30.080
I'm sorry I was about to
burn the village down

13:30.080 --> 13:32.710
because I thought my dad
was having an affair.

13:32.920 --> 13:35.920
And I'm sorry that I was about to
obliterate the insolent man

13:35.920 --> 13:37.920
who pointed a spear at my daughter.

13:37.920 --> 13:38.960
They're scary!

13:39.130 --> 13:41.830
Well, I guess everything's settled now.

13:41.830 --> 13:45.630
But dear, you still shouldn't be
sneaking out to get drunk like that.

13:45.630 --> 13:47.130
What are you talking about?!

13:47.130 --> 13:49.790
That's right.
You get out of hand when you drink!

13:49.790 --> 13:52.880
Well, I'm just glad to see that
they're getting along.

13:53.500 --> 13:55.170
Okay, see you later.

13:55.170 --> 13:56.170
Yeah.

13:58.170 --> 14:00.210
Do you understand what I was doing now?

14:00.210 --> 14:01.210
Yes.

14:02.540 --> 14:06.630
Our relationship with this village
is of the utmost importance.

14:07.000 --> 14:08.830
Despite their lack of numbers,

14:08.830 --> 14:11.920
they still have the power necessary
to challenge us.

14:11.920 --> 14:15.210
I never thought we'd meet anyone
that had the strength to overwhelm us.

14:15.210 --> 14:16.380
You're right...

14:16.670 --> 14:20.380
You couldn't even defend against that attack.
You had to avoid it.

14:20.750 --> 14:22.920
Even that was only thanks to the spider.

14:22.920 --> 14:23.830
Spider?

14:23.830 --> 14:26.210
Yes. An old friend of mine.

14:27.040 --> 14:31.630
Had I not been pulled out of the way;
I may not be standing here now.

14:32.040 --> 14:32.880
Lasty.

14:32.880 --> 14:33.960
Y-yes?

14:33.960 --> 14:36.670
I have a very important job for you.

14:37.460 --> 14:39.670
I want you to live here for a while.

14:40.540 --> 14:41.710
Mother?

14:41.710 --> 14:43.290
Wh-where's this coming from?

14:43.290 --> 14:45.210
Please keep your mouth shut, darling.

14:45.210 --> 14:46.040
Okay.

14:46.040 --> 14:48.420
We can't ignore that kind of power.

14:48.830 --> 14:51.040
I don't expect you to be able to suppress it,

14:51.040 --> 14:53.130
I just expect you to do your duty

14:53.130 --> 14:55.580
and make sure that such power
is never turned against us dragons.

14:55.580 --> 14:56.790
Is that understood?

14:57.290 --> 14:59.710
Yes. I'll do my best.

15:00.000 --> 15:01.330
Are you sure about this?

15:01.330 --> 15:06.250
Yes. I believe that choosing this path
will lead to the best outcome for Lasty.

15:06.250 --> 15:07.920
I can feel it.

15:08.960 --> 15:12.130
Sure, I don't mind.

15:12.330 --> 15:14.330
I look forward to working together!

15:14.330 --> 15:16.960
If you wouldn't mind,
please call me Lasty!

15:16.960 --> 15:18.630
Yeah, sounds good.

15:18.830 --> 15:20.960
So, what should I do here?

15:20.960 --> 15:22.750
Let's see...
And so, Lasty immediately<b>
</b>went to work in the village.<b></b>

15:22.750 --> 15:24.710
How about you start helping
with the harvesting?
And so, Lasty immediately<b>
</b>went to work in the village.<b></b>

15:25.540 --> 15:27.130
I'm ready to start now!

15:27.540 --> 15:29.920
A-are you a dragon?

15:30.420 --> 15:31.500
However...

15:32.670 --> 15:33.670
Huh?

15:36.670 --> 15:39.380
...dragons are pretty extraordinary
in all regards.

15:39.710 --> 15:41.040
Gently...

15:41.210 --> 15:42.710
Gently...

15:49.710 --> 15:52.880
It looks like it'll take a while
for her to get used to her work.

15:55.210 --> 15:56.130
Wait up!

15:56.130 --> 15:58.080
What should we do with her?

15:58.420 --> 16:01.540
Well, you don't need to make her do
something she isn't a fit for.

16:02.250 --> 16:05.750
But Dryme told me to give her work
to do around here.

16:07.250 --> 16:08.290
What is it?

16:08.290 --> 16:11.630
They've been like this ever since
all the dragons showed up here.

16:11.920 --> 16:15.130
The cows and chickens
have all be scared, too.

16:15.130 --> 16:17.290
